{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Of Asher.</b> Some say the mem is added, and the correct view in my eyes is that it is the land of Asher, whence comes bread and oil, and the word לחם is feminine, and likewise בית and מקום and יד and אש and עין and רוח and ארץ and ארון and עם," "and the meaning of מעדני מלך is known, and likewise Moses said, \"and he dips his foot in oil\" (Deuteronomy 33:24):"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {0 "Resolved abbreviation י\"א as 'some say'; the trailing list of feminine-gendered nouns ends with a comma, indicating the sentence continues into the next comment."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:32.389302333Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}